WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.255
Every flat shape has a name,
and the sides tell you which.

2
00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:13.444
Shapes fold in half, flip over a mirror,
and have a distance round the edge.

3
00:00:13.944 --> 00:00:17.566
A flat shape is named by how
many straight sides it has.

4
00:00:17.786 --> 00:00:21.780
Three straight sides and three
corners. That is a triangle.

5
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.365
Four straight sides make a
quadrilateral. A square is one.

6
00:00:26.585 --> 00:00:30.161
Five sides is a pentagon.
Six sides is a hexagon.

7
00:00:30.381 --> 00:00:34.421
Stand a square on its corner. It
is still a square, not a diamond.

8
00:00:34.921 --> 00:00:39.751
Regular means every side is the
same length, and every corner too.

9
00:00:39.971 --> 00:00:43.825
Both of these have five sides,
so both of them are pentagons.

10
00:00:44.045 --> 00:00:47.482
Only one of them is regular.
The other is stretched.

11
00:00:47.702 --> 00:00:51.696
Irregular is not wrong. Most
shapes around you are irregular.

12
00:00:52.196 --> 00:00:55.911
A line of symmetry is a fold
line, drawn on the shape.

13
00:00:56.131 --> 00:00:59.707
Fold along it, and the two
halves land on top of each other.

14
00:00:59.927 --> 00:01:03.781
Count them with me. A square
has four lines of symmetry.

15
00:01:04.001 --> 00:01:07.624
A rectangle has only two:
down the middle, and across.

16
00:01:07.844 --> 00:01:11.559
Cutting a shape in two is not
enough. The halves must match.

17
00:01:12.059 --> 00:01:15.263
A reflection flips a
shape over a mirror line.

18
00:01:15.483 --> 00:01:19.013
Every square lands the same
distance on the other side.

19
00:01:19.233 --> 00:01:23.459
This square is two along. Its
reflection is two along as well.

20
00:01:23.679 --> 00:01:27.626
Four squares on this side,
so four squares on that side.

21
00:01:27.846 --> 00:01:31.886
A reflection is not a slide.
It turns the shape round.

22
00:01:32.386 --> 00:01:35.869
A solid shape is not
flat. This one is a cube.

23
00:01:36.089 --> 00:01:39.805
A face is a flat surface.
A cube has six faces.

24
00:01:40.025 --> 00:01:44.158
An edge is where two faces
meet. A cube has twelve edges.

25
00:01:44.378 --> 00:01:48.557
A corner is where edges meet.
A cube has eight corners.

26
00:01:48.777 --> 00:01:53.468
The drawing is flat. Three edges
hide round the back. Count those too.

27
00:01:53.968 --> 00:01:57.358
Perimeter is the whole distance
round the outside edge.

28
00:01:57.578 --> 00:02:01.107
This rectangle is six
centimetres by two centimetres.

29
00:02:01.327 --> 00:02:05.460
Only two numbers are written on
it. The other two sides match.

30
00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:09.442
Six plus two plus six plus
two makes sixteen centimetres.

31
00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:14.492
Area is different. It is the
space inside, counted in squares.

32
00:02:14.712 --> 00:02:18.891
Twelve squares inside, and sixteen
centimetres round the edge.

33
00:02:19.391 --> 00:02:24.871
Count the sides to name a flat shape.
Regular means every side the same.

34
00:02:25.091 --> 00:02:30.293
A line of symmetry folds a shape
onto itself. A reflection flips it.

35
00:02:30.513 --> 00:02:34.228
A cube has six faces, twelve
edges and eight corners.

36
00:02:34.448 --> 00:02:38.209
Perimeter goes round the edge.
Area is the space inside.
